From 48460f28da27127e5382b0c08a13fffd0e6c6ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zain Ansari <900381+zainussami@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 00:19:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vmm: restore: allow net fd rebind for tap-name-mode devices

net_fds restore only rebound devices that were fd-backed at snapshot
time; tap-name-mode devices (fds: None) kept their serialized tap name,
so restoring a snapshot while another sandbox held that tap failed with
an opaque 'ConfigureTap: EBUSY' deep inside VM restore. This blocks
concurrent restore of the same snapshot, which is the scale-out path
(one template snapshot, N concurrent restores).

When the restore request supplies fresh queue fds for a tap-name-mode
device, rebind it: clone the fds and clear the tap name so the device
builder takes the fd-backed branch. Guarded by an fd-count*2 ==
num_queues match (num_queues counts virtqueues); mismatched counts keep
the previous behavior.

Legacy snapshots (pre-id tap-name devices) are handled host-side:
sandboxer's config rewrite normalizes their net device id to _net0
before CH sees the state, so the rebind matches regardless of snapshot
age.
---
 vmm/src/lib.rs | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vmm/src/lib.rs b/vmm/src/lib.rs
index dcf6614..be7d659 100644
--- a/vmm/src/lib.rs
+++ b/vmm/src/lib.rs
@@ -1762,6 +1762,23 @@ impl RequestHandler for Vmm {
                     // update only if the net dev is backed by FDs
                     if net_config.id.as_ref() == Some(&net.id) && net_config.fds.is_some() {
                         net_config.fds.clone_from(&net.fds);
+                    } else if net_config.id.as_ref() == Some(&net.id)
+                        && net_config.fds.is_none()
+                        && net_config.tap.is_some()
+                        && net
+                            .fds
+                            .as_ref()
+                            .map_or(false, |fds| fds.len() * 2 == net_config.num_queues)
+                    {
+                        // A tap-name-mode device (fds: None) can also be
+                        // rebound at restore: the serialized tap name may be
+                        // held by another sandbox when the same snapshot is
+                        // restored concurrently. Clear the tap so the device
+                        // builder takes the fd-backed branch with the fresh
+                        // queue fds instead of failing with a bare
+                        // ConfigureTap EBUSY after VM state load.
+                        net_config.fds.clone_from(&net.fds);
+                        net_config.tap = None;
                     }
                 }
             }
